{
 "id": "kyc_document_chase",
 "request": "Every day at 8am, go through the 'open' and 'restricted' requests in ops_db kyc_requests, with how many days each has been open (work it out in the query from requested_on, as days_open). For each request, first ask the document service whether the customer has uploaded the documents. If they have: set the request to 'complete', lift the restriction through core banking if it was 'restricted', and email the customer a thank-you. If not: from day 3 with no reminder sent yet, email the first reminder and set reminders_sent to 1; from day 7 with one reminder sent, email the second reminder and set reminders_sent to 2; from day 10 with two reminders sent and still 'open', restrict the customer through core banking, set status 'restricted', email the customer that their accounts are restricted, and email RM_EMAIL to call them. Otherwise leave that request alone. At the end, if anything happened, email KYC_TEAM_EMAIL one summary with how many were completed, reminded and restricted.",
 "apis": [
  "dms.yaml",
  "accounts.yaml"
 ],
 "tables": {},
 "expect": {
  "trigger": "Cron",
  "must_have_types": [
   "Postgres",
   "SendEmail"
  ],
  "must_call": [
   "dms.documents",
   "accounts.restrictCustomer",
   "accounts.liftRestriction"
  ],
  "max_nodes": 30
 },
